Dear all,

Day 4 of the serialised public record in this matter is attached. It places=
 before you a documentary contradiction that can be verified in 60 seconds a=
gainst the attached record.

During the ten-day final hearing in BV20D01752 (19=E2=80=9328 February 2024), my =
autism and Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder were referenced at least 25 times =
during the proceedings, including by the trial judge himself. The 111-paragr=
aph judgment that followed contains no reference to autism, PTSD, disability=
, vulnerability, participation measures, or mental health.

Paragraph 64 of the judgment replaced the clinical explanation identified d=
uring trial with a moral characterisation. Approximately =C2=A31,055,654.50 in f=
ixed costs, together with an indemnity costs order, have been imposed on the=
 basis of that characterisation. The recusal application brought to challeng=
e the pattern has remained undetermined for 454 days.

The attached catalogue of the 25 in-trial references identifies the speaker=
, day of trial, context, and verbatim quote where recorded.

Three things are sought:
First. Production, at public expense, of the transcripts of the final heari=
ng of 19=E2=80=9328 February 2024 and the hearing of 8 May 2025.
Second. Independent specialist review of the judgments of 18 April 2024 ([2=
024] EWFC 79), 24 May 2024 ([2024] EWFC 114), and 8 May 2025 against those t=
ranscripts and the underlying documentary record.
Third. Withdrawal of the judgments of 18 April 2024 and 24 May 2024 from th=
e National Archives and BAILII pending that review.
You are not asked to take a position on the litigation. You are placed on n=
otice of a documentary record capable of independent verification against th=
e attached material.

Access to counsel. The matters set out in the attached statement require re=
presentation by a public law specialist with experience in disability discri=
mination, judicial conduct, and institutional accountability.

I have prepared the documentary record underlying Days 1=E2=80=934 of this serial=
ised public record as a litigant in person, without representation, while fa=
cing liabilities exceeding =C2=A31 million arising from the proceedings describe=
d in the attached statement.

My health has materially deteriorated over the past 27 months and I remain =
under intensive specialist NHS care. The level of forensic and procedural wo=
rk required is no longer sustainable without specialist legal support.

The review of the judgments identified in the attached statement, against t=
he underlying trial transcripts and documentary record, now requires special=
ist counsel. Introductions, recommendations, or expressions of interest from=
 chambers or firms with relevant expertise would be welcomed.

Day 1 (20 April 2026), Day 2 (1 May 2026) and Day 3 (4 May 2026) are availa=
ble in the public archive: https://github.com/nadiazahmoul/Zahmoul-v-SSJ-HMC=
TS-Public-Archive

=20

Kind regards,

Nadia Zahmoul=20

Litigant in Person=20

nadia@rosekross.com=20

11 May 2026

